{{!< default}}
{{!-- WHS Brief: public Change Tracker (/tracker/).

Not to be confused with /register/ (register.hbs), which is paid-member-only
and shows full item content grouped by jurisdiction. This page stays public
and headline-only, but unlike the original version of this page, only a
handful of the most recent items are shown in full — the rest sit behind a
subscribe nudge. This is a deliberate conversion tradeoff (drive visitors to
subscribe) traded against the doc's original "give the whole list away free,
it's the best SEO asset" framing. To keep some of that SEO value despite the
gate, every item is still rendered into the real DOM (nothing is loaded only
on click, nothing is server-side member-gated the way /register/ is) — the
gate is a CSS max-height + fade + overlay CTA over content that's genuinely
present in the page source, not content withheld from it. The 9
/jurisdiction/{slug}/ pages are untouched by this and still show their full
list openly, since each is a smaller, targeted long-tail SEO landing page,
not "give away the whole store" in the way the all-jurisdictions view was.

How this works:
  - Each week, whs-legislative-brief-weekly creates/updates one small ALWAYS-
    PUBLIC post tagged #tracker (visibility: public, never paid) containing
    just compact .wbd-tracker-item entries (headline link + date + status,
    no description). This page fetches the last ~52 of those posts (roughly
    12 months at one per week) into a hidden container, and tracker.js (see
    assets/js/tracker.js) walks it, flattens every .wbd-tracker-item across
    all of them into one list, sorts newest first, and caps display to the
    last 12 months.
  - tracker.js then splits that list three ways: aggregate counts feed the
    snapshot stat tiles and jurisdiction chips, the first 5 items render in
    full into #wbd-tracker-preview, and everything after that renders into
    #wbd-tracker-output inside the fade-gated wrapper.
  - The 5-item cap only applies to anonymous visitors. Signed-in members
    (@member, free or paid, checked server-side below and passed to
    tracker.js via data-member) get every item in the open, uncapped, no
    fade, no CTA -- this was missing in an earlier version, where the gate
    applied unconditionally regardless of membership, so a member who'd
    actually signed up saw no payoff at all. "Subscribe" via the Portal
    button can land someone on the free tier, and free tier is enough to
    unlock this (the analysis behind the paid #brief post is the actual
    product, this is still just headline + date).
  - There is deliberately NO jurisdiction filter/nav row on this page anymore
    (an earlier version had one). Most of those links pointed straight at the
    9 /jurisdiction/{slug}/ pages, which show their full list completely in
    the open with no gate at all — so a visitor could click straight through
    a "filter" and see everything for free, defeating the whole point of the
    gate on this page. The "By jurisdiction" chips inside the snapshot below
    give the same at-a-glance breakdown (with real counts) without being
    clickable escape hatches. If jurisdiction pages get their own gate later,
    reintroducing real links here would make sense again; until then, don't.
--}}

<main id="site-main" class="site-main outer">
<div class="inner posts">

    <div class="whs-brief-doc" data-member="{{#if @member}}true{{else}}false{{/if}}">
        <div class="wbd-masthead">
            <p class="wbd-eyebrow">Work Health &amp; Safety — Change Tracker</p>
            <h1>Every WHS/OHS legislative change, tracked</h1>
            <p class="wbd-dek">Every Act, Regulation, Code of practice and Standard change we've covered in the last 12 months across Australia and New Zealand. Headline and date only — for the full story on any item, including what it means and what to do about it, see the weekly brief.</p>
        </div>

        {{!-- Everything below must stay INSIDE this .whs-brief-doc wrapper,
        not after it closes — the --wbd-* custom properties (--wbd-rule,
        --wbd-ink-soft, --wbd-accent, etc.) used throughout this page's CSS
        are scoped to .whs-brief-doc, not :root (see screen.css ~line 3265).
        Outside this wrapper those var() references resolve to nothing. --}}

        {{!-- Live snapshot: stat tiles + jurisdiction chips, computed by
        tracker.js from the same data as everything else on this page. --}}
        <div id="wbd-tracker-snapshot" class="wbd-tracker-snapshot">
            <p class="wbd-tracker-loading">Loading snapshot…</p>
        </div>

        <h2 class="wbd-tracker-subhead" id="wbd-tracker-subhead">{{#if @member}}All tracked changes{{else}}Recently added{{/if}}</h2>
        <div id="wbd-tracker-preview" class="wbd-tracker-preview"></div>

        {{!-- The clipped preview and the CTA card are separate elements in
        normal document flow, not one absolutely-positioned over the other —
        an earlier version put the CTA inside .wbd-tracker-gated with
        position:absolute, and its real rendered height (heading + body +
        button) exceeded the fade zone, so it overlapped directly on top of
        still-readable list text instead of covering it. Keeping them as
        siblings makes that impossible regardless of how tall the CTA copy
        or any given headline ends up being. --}}
        <div class="wbd-tracker-gated{{#if @member}} wbd-tracker-gated-open{{/if}}" id="wbd-tracker-gated">
            <div id="wbd-tracker-output" class="wbd-tracker-output"></div>
            <div class="wbd-tracker-fade"></div>
        </div>
        {{!-- Signed-in members (free or paid) never see this markup at all,
        not even briefly before tracker.js hides it -- checked server-side
        so there's no flash of "Subscribe" for someone who already has. --}}
        {{#unless @member}}
        <div class="wbd-tracker-cta">
            <p class="wbd-tracker-cta-head">See every tracked change</p>
            <p class="wbd-tracker-cta-body">Subscribe to browse the complete list across all nine Australian jurisdictions, New Zealand and Standards, not just the five most recent.</p>
            <a class="wbd-tracker-cta-btn" data-portal="signup">Subscribe</a>
        </div>
        {{/unless}}

        <p class="wbd-register-footnote">Want the analysis, not just the headline? <a href="{{@site.url}}/brief/">Subscribe to the full weekly brief</a>.</p>

        {{!-- Hidden source data: full content of recent #tracker posts, for
        tracker.js to parse. Never shown directly. --}}
        <div id="wbd-tracker-source" hidden>
            {{#get "posts" filter="tag:tracker" limit="52" order="published_at desc" as |posts|}}
                {{#foreach posts}}
                    {{content}}
                {{/foreach}}
            {{/get}}
        </div>
    </div>

</div>
</main>
